@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
@type = "koroneiki"

Feature: Koroneiki Account and Customer Contact API
	Testing Koroneiki Account API functionality in relation to Customer Contacts.

Teardown:
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following names
	| Koroneiki Auto Subsidiary |
	| Koroneiki Engr Subsidiary |
	| Koroneiki Automotive      |
	| Koroneiki Engineering     |
	* I tear down the contacts on koroneiki with the following email addresses
	| koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| koroneiki.contact2@lrcustomer.com.broken |

Scenario: Assign customer contact to account
	Koroneiki customer contacts should be able to be assigned to accounts.

	Given I create a contact on koroneiki with the following values
	| Email Address | koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | Koroneiki                                |
	| Language      | English                                  |
	| Last Name     | Contact1                                 |
	| Middle Name   | User                                     |
	And I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code         | KORAUTO                              | |
	| Description  | Test automotive account on koroneiki | |
	| Fax Number   | 555-555-1234                         | |
	| Name         | Koroneiki Automotive                 | |
	| Phone Number | 555-555-5678                         | |
	| Region       | United States                        | |
	| Status       | Active                               | |
	| Tier         | T4                                   | |
	| Website      | www.koroneikiautomotive.com          | |
	And I assign customer contacts with the following email addresses to the account "Koroneiki Automotive"
	| koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	Then the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be assigned the account "Koroneiki Automotive"
	And the customer contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be assigned the account "Koroneiki Automotive"
	And the customer contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be visible via nested field on the account "Koroneiki Automotive"
	And the account with the name "Koroneiki Automotive" should be assigned the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken"
	And the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be assigned the team "Koroneiki Automotive"

Scenario: Assign customer contact to account with special characters
	Koroneiki customer contacts should be able to be assigned to accounts with special characters in the description.

	Given I create a contact on koroneiki with the following values
	| Email Address | koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | Koroneiki                                |
	| Language      | English                                  |
	| Last Name     | Contact1                                 |
	| Middle Name   | User                                     |
	And I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code                  | KORAUTO                                                       | |
	| Description           | 100% $$$$$ making & awesome org for our @customers! ^_^ v +-= | |
	| Fax Number            | 555-555-1234                                                  | |
	| Name                  | Koroneiki Automotive                                          | |
	| Phone Number          | 555-555-5678                                                  | |
	| Profile Email Address | koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken                      | |
	| Region                | United States                                                 | |
	| Status                | Active                                                        | |
	| Tier                  | T4                                                            | |
	| Website               | www.koroneikiautomotive.com                                   | |
	And I assign customer contacts with the following email addresses to the account "Koroneiki Automotive"
	| koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	Then the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be assigned the account "Koroneiki Automotive"
	And the customer contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be assigned the account "Koroneiki Automotive"
	And the customer contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be visible via nested field on the account "Koroneiki Automotive"
	And the account with the name "Koroneiki Automotive" should be assigned the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken"
	And the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be assigned the team "Koroneiki Automotive"

Scenario: Assign nonexistent customer contact to account
	Koroneiki customer contacts should be able to be created and assigned to accounts if the contact does not exist.

	Given I create a nested field for a nonexistent customer contact with the following values
	| Email Address | koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | Koroneiki                                |
	| Language      | English                                  |
	| Last Name     | Contact1                                 |
	| Middle Name   | User                                     |
	And I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code                 | KORAUTO                              | |
	| Contact Nested Field | ${staticContactsNestedField}         | |
	| Description          | Test automotive account on koroneiki | |
	| Fax Number           | 555-555-1234                         | |
	| Name                 | Koroneiki Automotive                 | |
	| Phone Number         | 555-555-5678                         | |
	| Region               | United States                        | |
	| Status               | Active                               | |
	| Tier                 | T4                                   | |
	| Website              | www.koroneikiautomotive.com          | |
	Then the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be assigned the account "Koroneiki Automotive"
	And the customer contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be assigned the account "Koroneiki Automotive"
	And the customer contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be visible via nested field on the account "Koroneiki Automotive"
	And I should be able to view a koroneiki contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" and the following values
	| Email Address | koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | Koroneiki                                |
	| Language      | English                                  |
	| Last Name     | Contact1                                 |
	| Middle Name   | User                                     |
	And the account with the name "Koroneiki Automotive" should be assigned the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken"
	And the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be assigned the team "Koroneiki Automotive"

Scenario: Assign nonexistent verified customer contact to account
	Koroneiki verified customer contacts should be able to be created and assigned to accounts if the contact does not exist.

	Given I create a nested field for a nonexistent customer contact with the following values
	| Email Address          | koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| Email Address Verified | true                                     |
	| First Name             | Koroneiki                                |
	| Language               | English                                  |
	| Last Name              | Contact1                                 |
	| Middle Name            | User                                     |
	And I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
